# dispatch-pretooluse.manifest — the rules each PreToolUse chain runs, in order.
#
# Format:  <chain-key>|<script basename>
#
# ORDER IS THE ORDER hooks.json REGISTERED THEM. It decides the order refusals
# are read back in, which is the only thing order can decide here: every module
# runs on every call regardless of what any other module returns, exactly as
# the host ran the separate registrations.
#
# These are the SAME FILES that used to be registered individually. They were
# not moved and not edited; they are simply no longer spawned one process each.
# A module stays independently runnable — `bash scripts/hooks/<module> < payload`
# still works and is what each module's own test suite does.
#
# THREE SCRIPTS THAT BELONG TO THESE EVENTS ARE DELIBERATELY NOT HERE:
#   shell-evidence.sh      an input transformer (returns updatedInput), not a
#                          rule; still registered on PreToolUse[Bash] directly.
#   dialect-guard.sh       the same reason on the Write chain: it returns
#                          updatedInput (American spelling fixed in the write)
#                          as well as refusing, so it is registered on
#                          PreToolUse[Write|Edit|MultiEdit|NotebookEdit] directly.
#   guard-sealed-worktree.sh  registered on the EMPTY matcher, so it governs
#                          every tool. Listing it under Bash-or-Write would
#                          narrow what it protects.
#
# ADDING A RULE: add the line here and nothing else. It does NOT go into
# hooks.json — the dispatcher is what hooks.json registers. Removing a rule is
# the same edit backwards, which is the point: the design this implements was
# written because removing a hook cost seventeen edits and adding one cost two.

Bash|guard-interactive-prompt.sh
Bash|guard-bash-main-writes.sh
Bash|guard-inflight-notify.sh
Bash|guard-worktree-removal.sh
Bash|guard-publication-commits.sh
Bash|guard-named-persons-commands.sh
Bash|guard-ceo-todos-commits.sh
Bash|guard-completeness-commits.sh
Bash|guard-row-currency-commits.sh
Bash|guard-vendoring-commits.sh
Bash|guard-hook-registration-commits.sh
Bash|guard-ci-red-lands.sh
Bash|guard-host-display-power.sh
Bash|guard-public-record-repo.sh
Bash|guard-land-lease-commands.sh
Bash|guard-foreign-app-data.sh
Bash|guard-unguarded-rm.sh
Bash|guard-host-sleep.sh
Bash|guard-operator-claim.sh
Bash|guard-shared-scratchpad.sh
Bash|guard-no-shell-c.sh

Write|guard-main-checkout-writes.sh
Write|scan-secrets.sh
Write|guard-publication-writes.sh
Write|guard-named-persons-writes.sh
Write|guard-no-home-network-phone.sh
Write|guard-host-display-power.sh
Write|guard-operator-claim.sh
Write|guard-shared-writes.sh
Write|guard-record-owner-memory.sh
